[NTST.13.3] **A case's failures are a closed set.** Besides an assertion whose
count does not satisfy it, a case fails for exactly these reasons, and the
report names each by its kind:

- an outbound call that no `TestResponse` stub answers ([RTIM.14.6]);
- a `Test*` or `Oracle*` atom the runtime did not understand or did not
  evaluate ([RTIM.14.9]);
- a step of the drive the engine refused without halting ([RTIM.14.14]), the
  step and its status in the detail;
- the engine halting during the case ([NCBK.2.9]), the fault in the detail;
- the case's own engine not created or not loaded, the status in the detail.

The kinds are a registry ([STYL.5.9.7]), allocated with the first runtime that
reports them.
